}# C30 remediation after attempt-03 (8/7/8/8/7, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 established coverage gaps discarded | A Runtime source counts as read only when it established what it is for: `RuntimeOverview::chart_established` (read, consistent totals) and `keys_established` (read, whole, no unreported expiration), defined beside the gap producers in `observation.rs`; Gateway usage only when `activity_known()` (requests and errors both known). Each shortfall is named in `sourcesMissing`, so the completion toast and the Inbox gap agree. Test: `ui_v2_inbox::established_coverage_not_mere_answers_counts_as_read` (an unreported key expiration; inconsistent chart totals; healthy answers stay complete) | `observation.rs`, `inbox_domain.rs` |
| R2 failed product attempts replaced outcomes and invented read times | `OverviewRecord` keeps, per product, the last outcome that established at least one source and, separately, the latest `FailedAttempt` (every source failed, or the read never reached the service); `settle_product` never lets a failure replace an outcome. `ReadStatus`: `lastReadAt` only from established reads, `failedAt` from the latest failures, state `failed` while a non-role failure is the latest attempt of any chosen product; the product entry reports the failure and names the kept older read. Test: `ui_v2_inbox::a_failed_product_attempt_is_reported_and_never_replaces_its_last_read` | `observation_domain.rs`, `inbox_domain.rs` |
| R3 Home all-clear during a first in-progress read | `attentionEmpty`: "Reading…" while the first read is open, the failure line when failed, "Nothing needs action in what was read. N sources were not read." when partial, the all-clear only after a complete read. Test: `inbox.test` (reading, partial, complete) | `home.tsx`, `copy.ts` |
| R4 tenant-owned toasts global | `Toast.tenant`: read completions, snooze receipts, rechecks and context-bound action outcomes speak for the tenant they were raised in; the shell retires them on leaving that tenant (`retireToasts`), with or without Reduce Motion; a returned tenant's old receipt is a baseline, not news. Test: `inbox.test` (snooze toast under Reduce Motion gone after A → B, not re-announced back in A) | `store.ts`, `v2-shell.tsx`, `home.tsx`, `app.tsx`, `toasts.tsx` (unchanged render) |
| R5 admitted save racing a discard | The sink re-checks the discard tombstone under the history hold, after admission and before the write; the tombstone is written before the Discard job, which removes under the same hold, so an admitted save that acquires the hold after the removal refuses instead of writing the transcript back. Fixture builds expose a `save_gate` (held by a test between admission and write). Test: `harness_tools::a_save_admitted_before_a_discard_never_writes_the_discarded_transcript` (engine killed with the approval pending, its cut-short save held at the gate, Discard and switch, gate released: no record, not listed) | `harness_history.rs`, `harness/sidecar.rs`, `tests/harness_process/desk.rs` |
| R6 discard failure hidden by unrelated history work | An outstanding discard failure is re-applied as the workspace's `problem` after a successful open and after a removal of a different record; only the failed record's own removal clears it. Test: extension of `a_discard_whose_removal_fails_is_reported_until_the_record_is_removed` (open the record, delete another; still reported; then its removal clears it) | `harness_history.rs` |

B1/E1 (the C29 live Vulture verification receipt) stay owner-gated (`evidence/C29/live-scope-request.md`). The two retained fixture-suite flake logs record same-input retries of timing-sensitive Harness tests outside this chunk's scope.
